-- title:
--   §4, p. 12 — the procedure Fix(f, x, η): after $\lceil\log_2(n^3\eta/\kappa)\rceil$ phases, $\delta < \kappa/n^3$ and some $w \in Y$ lies in every minimizer
-- statement:
--   Let $V$ be a finite nonempty set with $|V| = n$, $f$ a real submodular function on $V$ with $f(\emptyset) = 0$, and $x \in B(f)$ the extreme base generated by a linear ordering $L$ of $V$, with $x(v) \le \eta$ for all $v \in V$, where $\eta > 0$. Let $\kappa > 0$ and $Y \subseteq V$ with $f(Y) \le -\kappa$. Apply the scaling algorithm starting with $\delta = \eta$, the single index $(L, 1)$ and $\varphi = 0$. Let a state be reached at the end of a phase after
--   $$K = \lceil \log_2(n^3\eta/\kappa) \rceil$$
--   scaling phases (so its $\delta$ equals $\eta/2^K$). Then $\delta < \kappa/n^3$, and some $w \in Y$ satisfies $x(w) < -n^2\delta$ and belongs to every minimizer of $f$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** This is the paragraph as printed. When $n^3\eta/\kappa$ is a power of $2$ the printed count gives $\delta = \kappa/n^3$ exactly (for $n = 1$, $f(\{a\}) = -1$, $\eta = 2$, $\kappa = 1$: one phase, $\delta = 1$, $x(a) = -1 = -n^2\delta$), so the statement is expected to be false. The variant `IwataFF.SFM.fix_finds_element_corrected` uses $\lfloor\log_2(n^3\eta/\kappa)\rfloor + 1$ phases. "After $K$ phases" is encoded as a reachable state at a phase end whose $\delta$ is $\eta/2^K$, since each phase start halves $\delta$ and nothing else changes it. $\lceil\cdot\rceil$ is `Nat.ceil` of `Real.logb 2`.
-- source:
--   Iwata, Fleischer & Fujishige, A Combinatorial, Strongly Polynomial-Time Algorithm for Minimizing Submodular Functions, arXiv:math/0004089v1, p. 12, §4 (the procedure Fix(f, x, η))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_IwataFF_SFM_Basic
import Definitions.Def_IwataFF_SFM_Phase

namespace IwataFF.SFM

/-- §4, p. 12 (arXiv:math/0004089v1), the procedure `Fix(f, x, η)`, as printed: after
`⌈log₂(n³η/κ)⌉` scaling phases started from `δ = η` and the extreme base `x` generated by `L`,
`δ < κ/n³`, and some `w ∈ Y` has `x(w) < −n²δ` and belongs to every minimizer of `f`. -/
theorem fix_finds_element {α : Type} [DecidableEq α] (V : Finset α) (hV : V.Nonempty)
    (f : Finset α → ℝ) (hsub : SubmodularOn V f) (hf0 : f ∅ = 0)
    (L : List α) (hL : IsOrdering V L) (η κ : ℝ) (hη : 0 < η)
    (hxη : ∀ v ∈ V, greedy f L v ≤ η) (hκ : 0 < κ)
    (Y : Finset α) (hY : Y ⊆ V) (hfY : f Y ≤ -κ)
    (st : PhaseState α) (hrun : Relation.ReflTransGen (ScStep f V) (initPhase L η) st)
    (hbeg : st.begun = true) (hend : PhaseEnd f V st)
    (hK : st.delta = η / 2 ^ ⌈Real.logb 2 ((V.card : ℝ) ^ 3 * η / κ)⌉₊) :
    st.delta < κ / (V.card : ℝ) ^ 3 ∧
      ∃ w ∈ Y, xOf f st w < -((V.card : ℝ) ^ 2) * st.delta ∧
        ∀ X : Finset α, IsMinimizer V f X → w ∈ X := by sorry

end IwataFF.SFM
